 /><zone xml:id="m-8afb66e0-b67a-41be-885b-381eacd9cfa3" ulx="35" uly="939" lrx="888" lry="978" /><zone xml:id="m-b1603fc6-b5ce-4e39-9982-c94261868d6a" ulx="177" uly="1026" lrx="812" lry="1068" /><zone xml:id="m-0fa139f1-4025-4609-9b00-e9eccbb6277b" ulx="60" uly="1110" lrx="956" lry="1148" /><zone xml:id="m-4232263d-fe57-47e4-8520-73615aa35d4d" ulx="28" uly="1139" lrx="955" lry="1181" /><zone xml:id="m-2874b10e-14f7-4207-a1dd-e2ecf1975800" ulx="30" uly="1168" lrx="435" lry="1208" /><zone xml:id="m-e428d091-bd34-4e64-859c-25e0bf2f30b8" ulx="58" uly="1208" lrx="957" lry="1252" /><zone xml:id="m-e97727bf-7d1f-409e-a6d3-b4afc08f4b1d" ulx="30" uly="1241" lrx="956" lry="1277" /><zone xml:id="m-6218eafc-6a4c-4012-8ff4-fe0b4b0b7f3a" ulx="28" uly="1269" lrx="870" lry="1302" /><zone xml:id="m-86dc1e8d-9ae2-47eb-bd84-3e80ef29e8dc" ulx="57" uly="1314" lrx="955" lry="1347" /><zone xml:id="m-bc621c2c-36b8-40c2-b807-8a7103088f4a" ulx="27" uly="1345" lrx="953" lry="1377" /><zone xml:id="m-5e960a8b-a148-4301-9021-64fd7b1bd78f" ulx="29" uly="1370" lrx="954" lry="1407" /><zone xml:id="m-cac3f610-750b-43b9-ae18-d453cfc88411" ulx="28" uly="1400" lrx="951" lry="1435" /><zone xml:id="m-15f4f1fd-fa65-438e-8de7-66729ee45741" ulx="62" uly="1439" lrx="397" lry="1482" /><zone xml:id="m-74adf4de-0889-45b8-b430-6c16ceb09922" ulx="526" uly="1440" lrx="853" lry="1483" /><zone xml:id="m-35c2976e-199a-4845-8178-e939b54f7067" ulx="150" uly="1500" lrx="281" lry="1540" /><zone xml:id="m-901e77af-9b13-4d13-b8f7-b8629a4a477d" ulx="736" uly="1509" lrx="837" lry="1545" /><zone xml:id="m-9019b628-1a2e-40fd-b159-8a42e427ee01" ulx="75" uly="1546" lrx="952" lry="1591" /><zone xml:id="m-91228def-bc17-4c9a-8b6b-61857b462ea7" ulx="31" uly="1581" lrx="952" lry="1620" /><zone xml:id="m-aeecde04-f51e-4ace-b729-abf0182cd3f8" ulx="28" uly="1611" lrx="951" lry="1653" /></surface></facsimile><body>
    <mdiv type="solesmes">
      <score>
        <section>
          <pb xml:id="m-96dfc808-8921-4f86-8026-0e1dbd653f83" n="0931" facs="#m-5347d188-7851-471d-9d4e-98e60229dc4c" /><div xml:id="m-75df2e1d-5b88-4a12-8619-d990288590e7">
            <lg xml:id="m-07bd9a93-5190-4711-a140-170373a13c16">
              <l xml:id="m-5b15c600-e736-4d40-9d8e-b523b7b3be22" facs="#m-9d138b66-2ef3-4372-a933-02fdf5159186" label="text-like">EASTER SUNDAY</l><l xml:id="m-bce85ebf-7000-44f4-aaf3-666690afb127" facs="#m-d6687f96-8546-408c-b3cb-2d3dd2fc6e36" label="text-like">Double of the First Class with privileged Octaue</l><l xml:id="m-d7ce1178-d1b9-4f0e-b1ca-c6e79341b9b3" facs="#m-da231c12-0645-4fbe-9064-c81b7f880131" label="text-like">THE PASCHAL VIGIL</l><l xml:id="m-7a19aec6-fb94-4051-b5f5-df8f051c3872" facs="#m-7fa4a43d-39cc-4e19-9892-54a129e4172a" label="ambiguous">Station ad St. John Lateran</l><l xml:id="m-670910a9-7e53-41fc-9bef-5c2e8463bd9f" facs="#m-a3f73788-b11c-4d86-acd8-a5a45af392a0" label="text-like">The plan and purpose of this Vigil is to signify and recall by the liturgy</l><l xml:id="m-3c646760-910e-4b3c-9b91-c36870ebd075" facs="#m-fc3789aa-aa34-4bab-acfa-87919aefff22" label="lyrics-like">how grãce and life sprang up for us from the death of our Lord.</l><l xml:id="m-c68c06b7-fb60-4e45-ae7f-7dfbd06fcbd9" facs="#m-62242a21-df0b-4533-be88-f6089a05853e" label="text-like">Thus our Lord himself — the light of the world, (John 8, 12) — is</l><l xml:id="m-718e2312-530f-47c3-bb69-f26ad3531095" facs="#m-a3ff2e68-a2be-4f12-b93b-838f1ec4b752" label="text-like">presented to us under the sign of the Paschal candle: for He has scattered</l><l xml:id="m-ca22c4af-2f4f-4800-9eb2-9bbfe0461315" facs="#m-9f709714-7c36-4868-aa4d-6e34a571fc39" label="text-like">the darkness of our sins by the grace of his light, p. 7761;</l><l xml:id="m-8e51a65a-f924-4170-8411-afe04087026d" facs="#m-bc66063d-299a-4f2e-a8a8-cbc4d50a9f19" label="text-like">Then the solemn Praise of Easter (Exsultet) is announced, describing</l><l xml:id="m-cf5061d6-1c12-48d7-80fc-f07036bbb376" facs="#m-671432f3-46a5-4b1b-a8c0-2dd6649c760e" label="text-like">the splendour of the holy night of the Resurrection, p. 776M;</l><l xml:id="m-32b63be3-fca4-4d74-8d34-71ed320c8272" facs="#m-df9a10da-01a8-470f-9691-1b3baff88171" label="text-like">Then are commemorated God's mighty works of the old Testament,</l><l xml:id="m-c8853ee9-1b14-41f5-b5d0-9118002326a8" facs="#m-1ea11445-9b55-43a1-9f5f-a4cf861b261e" label="text-like">which are pale images of the wonders of the New Testament, p. T76r;</l><l xml:id="m-5aaa70c5-026c-40a0-987b-f885a6a5857f" facs="#m-6223a871-3f82-40aa-afe0-a77336e8924a" label="text-like">The water of Baptism is blessed, in which, buried with Christ to die</l><l xml:id="m-3e4d535c-d1ec-4498-8338-03e297624e14" facs="#m-367b77bb-edfd-4b03-964e-1ded8912e048" label="text-like">to sin, we rise again with him to walk in a new life. (Rom. 6, 4.)</l><l xml:id="m-8c0875c1-3337-42ec-a50f-fb2a8219b9b7" facs="#m-73218c58-8397-4ecd-8f69-4d65398d38b6" label="ambiguous">p. T70x;</l><l xml:id="m-877121ea-170c-4233-9b8a-c39e1f6402b6" facs="#m-2560fd56-c11c-4abb-84e2-8351c69e9454" label="ambiguous">we then engage ourselves by renewing our Baptismal promises to</l><l xml:id="m-0c16a3be-e7b9-4bec-bee2-b525650c39f5" facs="#m-1e35a611-5e0a-4f51-a651-fdac64657716" label="text-like">bear witness before all men and in all our life to the grace which Christ</l><l xml:id="m-a1b1a5aa-622f-4e81-8499-58e69c847e94" facs="#m-b4f01193-02b3-4460-8e86-481e3faedc99" label="text-like">merited for us and conferred on us at Baptism, p. 776pb;</l><l xml:id="m-c661321a-a621-4080-a029-90e4afb18e3f" facs="#m-974cf3b1-22c7-41d4-9259-66b452f6207c" label="text-like">Lastly, after imploring the prayers of the Church triumphant, we end</l><l xml:id="m-2651414b-9978-4a5b-9a6a-cda4e5256aca" facs="#m-8afb66e0-b67a-41be-885b-381eacd9cfa3" label="text-like">the sacred Vigil with the solemn Mass of the Resurrection, p. T76Hn.</l><l xml:id="m-0a64fc33-43a9-4fef-9304-df3251a3caaf" facs="#m-b1603fc6-b5ce-4e39-9982-c94261868d6a" label="text-like">THE BLESSING OF THE NEW FIRE</l><l xml:id="m-8ef9cb47-93d9-4e38-b09b-41066d1e533d" facs="#m-0fa139f1-4025-4609-9b00-e9eccbb6277b" label="text-like">1. The altars are covered with cloths at a suitable time, but the candles</l><l xml:id="m-c3164fdc-8ee4-4a9b-9c01-58c2838512ab" facs="#m-4232263d-fe57-47e4-8520-73615aa35d4d" label="text-like">are not lit until ihe beginning of Mass. Meanhile fire is strucke from fint,</l><l xml:id="m-7308eb41-13f2-4de7-b67a-c2e26c600034" facs="#m-2874b10e-14f7-4207-a1dd-e2ecf1975800" label="text-like">and from this, charcoal is lighted.</l><l xml:id="m-c93eaa24-b4e6-4e32-a7ba-a01933a4fd23" facs="#m-e428d091-bd34-4e64-859c-25e0bf2f30b8" label="text-like">2. The celebrant is vested in amice, alb, girdle, purple stole and cope</l><l xml:id="m-eb077e15-94fa-4af5-954f-7363a67de3f6" facs="#m-e97727bf-7d1f-409e-a6d3-b4afc08f4b1d" label="text-like">tor vithout chasublel, the sacred ministers wear amice, alb and girdle, the</l><l xml:id="m-bac6eb5d-da8e-4264-9c4d-1fbefa001bd4" facs="#m-6218eafc-6a4c-4012-8ff4-fe0b4b0b7f3a" label="text-like">deacon a purple stole and dalmatic and the subdeacon a purple tunicle.</l><l xml:id="m-c9514875-958e-48f1-ae6f-f84be88b0ab4" facs="#m-86dc1e8d-9ae2-47eb-bd84-3e80ef29e8dc" label="text-like">3. The ministers Ior serversl assemble with cross, holy water and incense</l><l xml:id="m-8f0354ba-e49a-4586-ba46-e68e4785173a" facs="#m-bc621c2c-36b8-40c2-b807-8a7103088f4a" label="text-like">either at the door of the church, or in the porch, or even inside the church,</l><l xml:id="m-4043ff66-4520-4f61-a082-f01510b7dcbd" facs="#m-5e960a8b-a148-4301-9021-64fd7b1bd78f" label="text-like">vherever the people can best follow the ceremony, and the celebrant blesses the</l><l xml:id="m-c1cfdff7-1ce1-4ca7-aeb2-167a7b289ddd" facs="#m-cac3f610-750b-43b9-ae18-d453cfc88411" label="text-like">new fire, saving aohat follous to the ferial tone E Ior the simple ancient tonel:</l><l xml:id="m-58243856-6c6d-4d14-bfa8-43e7dfe6fa5e" facs="#m-15f4f1fd-fa65-438e-8de7-66729ee45741" label="lyrics-like">V. Dóminus vobíscum.</l><l xml:id="m-9596bfc0-6720-4c02-bf19-16f2c7596650" facs="#m-74adf4de-0889-45b8-b430-6c16ceb09922" label="lyrics-like">N. Et cum spíritu túo.</l><l xml:id="m-06d877ff-6c58-4160-8842-a19dd885ed1b" facs="#m-35c2976e-199a-4845-8178-e939b54f7067" label="lyrics-like">Orémus.</l><l xml:id="m-708a494a-c3bc-4455-9bdf-697525057766" facs="#m-901e77af-9b13-4d13-b8f7-b8629a4a477d" label="text-like">Prayer</l><l xml:id="m-4e37cad9-d6d5-45c0-b793-e2a168b62c36" facs="#m-9019b628-1a2e-40fd-b159-8a42e427ee01" label="lyrics-like">Eus, qui per Filium tuum, contulísti: prodúctum e silice,</l><l xml:id="m-7d284548-8b9a-4f47-b474-f5562c7e2c60" facs="#m-91228def-bc17-4c9a-8b6b-61857b462ea7" label="lyrics-like">U angulárem scilicet lápidem, nostris profutúrum úsibus, no¬</l><l xml:id="m-c414de52-2f91-456c-95b1-b67db81611ad" facs="#m-aeecde04-f51e-4ace-b729-abf0182cd3f8" label="lyrics-like">claritátis tuae ignem fidélibus! vum hunc ignem sancti 4 fica:</l></lg></div></section></score></mdiv></body></music>
</mei>